'''Ashpharim Dhey, the Saviour''' is a [[Rogue Psyker]] who serves the [[Thousand Sons]] in the [[Age of the Dark Imperium]].{{Fn|1}} 

He was once a member of the [[Sorcerer]] [[Amhot]]'s inner circle of [[Thrall Wizard|acolytes]], but was given a new role in the wake of [[Mankind]]'s [[Psychic Awakening]]{{Fn|1}}. As new [[Psyker]]s began to emerge throughout the [[Imperium]], Dhey was charged with saving them from being hunted down and killed. To do so, he would infiltrate Imperial worlds and offer psykers a safe haven, in the [[New Kingdom]] the [[Daemon Primarch]] [[Magnus]] was building in the [[Prospero System]]. If they accepted, Dhey requested that they show their loyalty to Magus by bearing the [[Cyclops' Mark]], which required them to cut out their right eye, in imitation of the Daemon Primarch. Once Dhey had gathered a significant amount of psykers, he would take them to his ship and begin the long journey back to the Prospero System{{Fn|2}}. A perilous journey many of these psykers would not survive, as they began training to use their powers.{{Fn|1}} 

