Aster Lydorran.wikitext:
{{ImperialFistsPortal}}
[[File:Fist-of-the-Imperium-clear.jpg|300px|thumb|Aster Lydorran {{fn|1c}}]]
'''Aster Lydorran''' is an [[Imperial Fists]] [[Primaris Librarian|Primaris]] [[Epistolary]], who serves in the [[Command Squad]] of [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Ercuros Tor]]'s [[5th Company (Imperial Fists)|Fifth Company]].{{Fn|1a}}
==History==
He was taken by agents of [[Magos Dominus|Archmagos Dominus]] [[Belisarius Cawl]] to become a [[Primaris Space Marine]] in [[M36]]. Lydorran later succeeded in becoming a [[Imperial Psychic Powers_#Imperial Fists|Geokinesis]]-styled [[Primaris Librarian|Primaris]] [[Epistolary]], descended from the [[Primarch]] [[Rogal Dorn]], and was then placed in [[Stasis]] beneath [[Mars]], with other Primaris Marines. He would remain there until [[M42]], when the Primaris were unleashed to aid the [[Imperium]], which was embattled due to the creation of the [[Great Rift]]. Upon his awakening, Lydorran was sent to join the [[Command Squad]] of [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Ercuros Tor]]'s [[5th Company (Imperial Fists)|Fifth Company]] and subsequently took part in the successful battles against the forces of [[Chaos]] on [[Osmal II]] and [[Shondarch]]. Sometime later, they would answer a dire [[Astropathic]] warning that a rebellion had broken out on [[Ghyre]] from the Fifth Company [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] [[Larrus Torgan]], who had been stationed on the important [[Mining World]]{{Fn|1b}}

One year and twenty-six cycles sidereal later, the Fifth Company arrived at Ghyre aboard the [[Strike Cruiser]] [[Wrathful]]. Upon arriving on its surface, Tor and the Command Squad met with the Mining World's [[Marshal (Imperial Guard)|High Marshal]] [[Anthonius Kallistus]], to begin planning Ghyre's defense. However before any words could be spoken, Lydorran sensed a sudden rush of kinetic energy and raised his [[psychic]] defenses to defend against the attack. It would be too late, though, and Captain Tor was slain by a [[sniper]]{{Fn|1a}}. In the subsequent mayhem that erupted, Lydorran discovered the sniper and killed her in vengeance for Tor's death, before she could escape. He would then take command of the Fifth Company, as they did battle with the [[Genestealer Cult|Genestealer]] [[Cult of the Wrything Wyrm]], which was revealed to be behind the rebellion on Ghyre and the death of Captain Tor.{{Fn|1b}}

In the ensuing war on Ghyre, Lydorran dismissed concerns by the Ghyrish [[Ecclesiarchy]] conclave about excessive collateral damage being caused by the Imperial Fists. The Genestealer Cultists were taking advantage of this to broadcast anti-Space Marine propaganda to bolster their support. Nonetheless, he took a more cautious approach, which led to the frustration of [[Company Champion]] [[Hastur]]. Hastur led a small team to a warehouse in the commercial district, intending to strike a decisive blow. However instead, his squad walks into a Cultist trap.{{Fn|1d}} Beset by disaster and Ecclesiarchy political machinations, a frustrated Lydorran was nonetheless able to learn from [[Deathwatch]] [[Watch Captain]] and [[Space Wolf]] [[Lothar Redfang]] that the [[Genestealer Patriarch]] was located beneath Klaratos [[Hive]].{{Fn|1e}}

Lydorran agreed with Redfang that the best approach was to launch a massive attack on Klaratos to draw out the Patriarch. The attack would leave their current base Hive Angelicus, resulting in both agreeing for the need for speed in the coming operation. However as the attack is being launched, Genestealer forces under the [[Genestealer Magus|Magus]] [[Jai]] attempted to detonate a biological weapon in Angelicus port to draw away Space Marines. Thanks to the sacrifice of [[Chaplain]] [[Storn]] and a group of [[Arbites]], the plot was foiled.{{Fn|1f}}

Lydorran and Redfang then launch attacks on Klaratos as a recovering Hastur holds off Genestealer attacks on Port Angelicus. Upon hearing of the attack, Lydorran blames Redfang for the disaster and the two came to blows. Ultimately, thanks to Redfang allowing him to be beaten without resistance, Lydorran was able to regain his composure. The two then learned that the Patriarch was likely instead under Hive Mastracha due to the origin of the biological bomb the Cultists attempt to detonate. Using orbital warships to deliver [[Lance]] strikes, Hive Mastracha's power generators overload and created a massive explosion. Lydorran and Redfang then descended into the breach deep into the nest of the Genestealer Cult.{{Fn|1g}}

In the final battle deep within the broodnest, Lydorran and the Deathwatch fight through fierce cultist resistance. Lydorran and Redfang then dueled the Patriarch together, killing it and causing the [[Broodmind]] of the cult to collapse.{{Fn|1h}} While the war on Ghyre ended in Imperial victory as a result, the cost was high.{{Fn|1i}}

