Astor Sabbathiel.wikitext:
{{OrdoHereticusPortal}}
[[Image:Sabbathiel.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Inquisitor Astor Sabbathiel]]
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is an [[Inquisitor]] of the [[Ordo Hereticus]], determined to expose the [[Dark Angels]] [[Chapter]] as the heretics she believes they are.{{Fn|1b}}


==Biography==
Sabbathiel first encountered the Dark Angels on [[Heorath]], where she witnessed one of the [[Fallen]] working with [[daemon]]s in the subterranean caverns. Believing the entire [[Chapter]] was corrupt, she vowed to expose their treachery to the [[Imperium]].{{Fn|3}}

Five decades later,{{Fn|3}} [[Sarasti|a daemonhost]] she keeps in the hold of her [[Inquisitorial Cruiser|ship]] informed her that the [[warp-storm]]s shrouding the [[Calaphrax Cluster]] had abated in for the first time in ten millennia, and the Dark Angels would seek to obfuscate the truth that might be discovered there.{{Fn|1a}} When she and her [[Inquisitorial Henchmen|retinue]] arrived in the [[Exyrion]] system, they investigated an orbital observation station, discovering the bodies of several Dark Angels fallen in battle.{{Fn|1c}} Sabbathiel identified the cause of death as [[bolter]]-fire as her acolyte Fitch detected the impact of the asteroid launched at the surface of  Exyrion - and the [[Iron Warriors]] fleet that had launched it.{{Fn|1d}} She departed to [[Quintus (Forest World)|Quintus]], where her daemonhost had shown her visions of a [[Chaos Cult]] apparently led by the [[Fallen|Dark Angels]].{{Fn|2a}} After slaughtering the cultists, she found an ancient suit of black Dark Angels [[power armour]] used as an icon of worship, but it fell into a chasm in the fallout from the [[Battle of Quintus]].{{Fn|2b}}

Convinced she had enough evidence to expose the Dark Angels, Sabbathiel summoned the [[Grey Knights]]. [[Justicar]] [[Leofric]], in the Calaphrax Cluster due to the visions of the [[Prognosticator (librarian)|Prognosticator]]s, agreed to meet with her and decided that her evidence was sufficient to merit investigation. Sabbathiel accompanied the Grey Knights as they demanded [[Space Marine Captain|Master]] [[Seraphus]] allow them to board his [[Battle Barge]] to conduct their investigation.{{Fn|3}}

Ultimately, Sabbathiel was apparently executed by Leofric after it became apparent that she was consorting with [[Daemon]]s.{{Fn|3a}} However she survived her wounds and was nursed back to health by the mysterious [[Tech-Priest]] [[Metik]], who revealed that 100 years had passed and it was now the [[Era Indomitus]].{{Fn|4}} Later she recruited a new retinue and searched the abandoned [[Ecclesiarchy]] world of [[Karsharat]]  in order to claim an ancient cybernetic weapon.{{Fn|5}}

