Astorax.wikitext:
{{IronWarriorsPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is a [[Chaos Sorcerer]] of the [[Iron Warriors]] capable of scrying the future in bones. He served as a seer to [[Chaos Lord|Lord]]s [[Korus]]{{Fn|1}} and [[Bartok]], but his abilities were dismissed as superstitious by the [[Fallen]] who took over the Warband.{{fn|2}}

==Biography==
[[Image:Astorax.jpg|thumb|right|300px|{{PAGENAME}}]]
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' served as a seer to [[Chaos Lord|Lord]] [[Korus]] when his [[Warband]] entered the [[Calaphrax Cluster]] to reclaim a lost weapon. He remained aboard their [[Battle Barge]] rather than participating in battle, sitting on a throne of bones in an ossuary chamber. Astorax said the bones told of great victory, of the enemy crawling from the earth like insects, and of war.{{fn|1}}

After Korus died in the [[Second Battle of Exyrion]], Astorax briefly served his successor, [[Bartok]], until he was killed by one of the [[Fallen]] brought aboard by [[Rendix]]. Astorax offered to read the bones for the Fallen, but his abilities were dismissed as unnecessary. When the Fallen revealed his plan to turn the [[Dark Angels]] from the [[Emperor of Mankind|False Emperor]] to the ways of [[Luther]], Astorax claimed the bones had showed him that this was predestined.{{fn|2}}

