Asubha.wikitext:
{{WorldEatersPortal}}

{{PAGENAME}} was a Legionary in the [[World Eaters]]' 15th Company.{{fn|1a}}

==Biography==
{{Spoiler|source=The Outcast Dead (Novel)}}
Along with his twin [[Subha]], Asubha was one of the Astartes assigned to the [[Crusader Host]] when the [[Horus Heresy]] broke out. At that point, [[Rogal Dorn]] ordered the Host be captured, and Yasu Nagasena led a force of 3,000 men to that aim, resulting in the surviving Astartes' imprisonment in [[Khangba Marwu]].{{fn|1b}}

He was one of the Astartes who escaped from the prison, and [[Atharva]] saw him as the "assassin" to his brother's "butcher".{{fn|1b}} More circumspect than his fellow World Eaters, he was willing to entertain the possibility that their Legion might not be worthy of their loyalty anymore.{{fn|1c}} Technically minded, he had been selected for [[Techmarine]] training before his assignment to the Host and was the one to figure out the hunters were spying on the [[Outcast Dead]] through [[Kai Zulane]]'s augmetic eyes.{{fn|1d}}

When the Palace's hunters assaulted the Temple of Woe where the Outcast Dead had cremated their fallen comrades, Asubha and his brother went against [[Saturnalia Princeps Carthagina]] of the [[Legio Custodes]]. After the Custodian killed Subha with several bolter shells in the chest, Asubha flew into a rage and managed a mutual kill before lying to die next to his brother.{{fn|1e}}

