Aurelius Jeriko Gantar.wikitext:
{{AdeptusCustodesPortal}}
'''Aurelius Jeriko Gantar''' is a member of the [[Adeptus Custodes]]' [[Emissaries Imperatus]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
[[Image:Aurelius.jpg|thumb|right|200px|{{PAGENAME}}{{Fn|1}}]]
He was originally serving as a [[Blade Champion]], when Gantar heard the [[Emperor]]'s voice. The [[Custodes]]' master was trying to guide him somewhere and this led Gantar to join the [[Emissaries Imperatus]]. Afterwards, he became a member of the Imperatus group [[Those Who Hear]], due to them being of similar minds. In order to interpret what the Emperor wanted them to do, the group enacted the Emissaries' [[Pysidian Analytic]], the [[Attafaetian Mediation]] and conducted the [[Debates of Epyst]]. This led the Emperor's guidance to become clear and the humbled Those Who Hear set off for [[Lier's Reach]].{{Fn|1}} 

Held by the forces of [[Chaos]], it could not be found on a [[Cartograph]] that was younger than 6,000 years old, but thanks to the [[Emperor]]'s guidance, the group found the world. It was there, that the thrice-cursed [[Mantle of Rue]] lay and [[Those Who Hear]] landed upon [[Lier's Reach]] to find it. In order to do so, Gantar asked the group to be silent, as he only wanted to hear the Emperor's voice. Those Who Hear complied and their master began to lead Gantar to the Mantle. As they journeyed there, the group cut down any of the forces of Chaos that tried to stop them. Eventually, though, Gantar found the Mantle and Those Who Hear then escaped from Lier's Reach.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Codex: Adeptus Custodes (9th Edition)]], pg. 35 - ''Emissaries Imperatus: Deeds of Legends''
