Auric Stormcloud.wikitext:
{{EldarPortal}}{{Heretic Tomes}}
[[Image:Stormcloud.JPG|thumb|right|Auric Stormcloud]]
'''Auric Stormcloud''' is a [[Farseer]] of the [[Line of Manan]] from [[Craftworld]] [[Ulthwé]].{{Fn|1a}} He is on a quest to stop the [[daemon prince]] [[Shaha Gaathon]]'s attempts to possess rogue trader [[Janus Darke]]. Auric is accompanied by his bodyguard and relative [[Athenys]]. Auric travels with Darke to the dead Eldar world of [[Belial IV]] to retrieve the [[Deathsword]] — an ancient and potent weapon, said to be an echo of the sword of [[Kaela Mensha Khaine]]. The sword supposedly has the ability to destroy daemons utterly rather than simply banishing them.{{Fn|1x}}

Auric is slain on Belial IV, but he had earlier put a [[spirit stone|soul-stone]] in Janus Darke's head under the pretense of it protecting Janus from daemonic possession. When Auric's own soul-stone was destroyed by the Daemon, his soul moved to the one in Janus's head, taking control of the body.{{Fn|1x}}

==Description==
Auric was taller than [[Athenys]]. While on [[Medusa (Hive World)|Medusa]] he wore a massive bulky black cloak trimmed with white fur, to try to blend in.{{Fn|1b}}

