Aurus (Captain).wikitext:
{{UltramarinesPortal}}
'''Aurus''' is a [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] in the [[Ultramarines]] [[Chapter]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
Earlier in his career, he led one of his [[Chapter]]'s strike forces to the [[Imperial]] colony of [[Persiphon]], which was being tormented by [[Drukhari]] raiders. The cruel [[Xenos]] lingered long enough for the [[Ultramarines]] to arrive and Aurus led the strike force to victory over the Drukhari. While the people of Persiphon were left feeling ashamed for not being able to defend themselves, as the [[God-Emperor]] demanded, they also felt a bone-deep veneration for the Ultramarines for saving them. This adulation soon became a desire to echo the [[Chapter]]'s strength and a vow that Persiphon would never need to be rescued again. This led the world's six great clans to established '''Halls of Excellence''', wherein aspirants would train to become the best warriors that [[Augmentic|unaugmented]] [[Human]]s could be. A spirit of healthy competition and deserved pride in their achievements saw the Halls turn out highly trained, physically conditioned and well-equipped warriors for the next two generations. These [[Guardsmen]]  marched out armored in blue and gold in honor of the Ultramarines. However the need for their own warriors to achieve perfection, eventually led to a civil war between the Halls in [[M42]].{{Fn|1}} 

[[Astropathic]] messages from the world would be sent out declaring the outbreak of the war and that unidentified [[Xenos]] monsters had also begun tormenting [[Persiphon]]'s population and as fate would have it, Aurus would once again lead a strike force to come to its aid. Before the [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] reached the world, though, he would be met by [[Inquisitor]] [[Rudran Luc]], who had heard the messages as well. Luc, however, had sought to investigate Persiphon beforehand, when whispers circulated about a deviant [[Six Circles|religion]] growing within the Halls of Excellence. The civil war prevented the Inquisitor from even beginning his investigations, but Luc suspected something more insidious was at work. When he learned that Captain Aurus was going to stop the war, the Inquisitor had rushed to meet him before the Ultramarines arrived at Persiphon. The two would then reach the world and the Inquisitor's worst fears were realized, as they saw that Persiphon was being invaded by the [[Daemon]]s of [[Slaanesh]]. Their interrogation of remote [[Augur|data-augur]]s revealed how the competition between the '''Halls of Excellence''', to train the best [[Guardsmen]], turned sour and plunged Perisiphon into a shockingly savage civil war. The need to achieve victory, later led each of the Halls' war clerics to appeal to [[Chaos|dark powers]] and caused the Daemons to invade Persiphon.{{Fn|1}} 

Chief among them were six [[Keepers of Secrets]], who each ruled a realm from a corrupted '''Hall of Excellence'''. Seeing such [[Heresy]] led the [[Ultramarines]] to launch an attack and on Aurus' orders, his forces separated so they could strike at different parts of [[Persiphon]]. Aurus invaded the '''Goahv Province''' and his target was the greatest of the Halls of Excellence, but upon entering it the Captain's forces found themselves scattered amidst a maze of distorted mirrors. As they ventured forth, whispered temptations drowned out the Ultramarines' [[vox]]es, and soporific incense seeped into their sealed [[power armour]]. All the while, [[Daemon]] of [[Slaanesh]] burst from the mirrors' every twisted reflection to attack the [[Space Marines]]. Meanwhile [[Inquisitor]] [[Rudran Luc|Luc]] had stayed in orbit and listened with growing dismay as Persiphon's debauched insanity converged on the outnumbered Ultramarines. He also watched the weave of the [[Warp]] thinning on the world and realized a huge Daemonic incursion threatened to appear on Persiphon. In response to this, Luc had his [[Astropath]]s immediately send an encoded summons to the [[Grey Knights]], as the [[Chapter]]'s strength would now be needed to defeat the Daemons.{{Fn|1}} 

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Codex: Chaos Daemons (9th Edition)]], pgs. 26-27 - ''War Zone: Persiphon''

