Averamus.wikitext:
__NOTOC__
{{DarkAngelsPortal}}
'''Averamus''' is a [[The Fallen|Fallen Angel]].{{Fn|1}}


==Biography==
Averamus was last seen collaborating with the [[Chaos Space Marine]]s of the [[Emperor's Children]] in their campaign to destabilise the [[Vensine Sector]]. While overseeing the actions of [[Sslyth]] mercenaries on [[Kolagar]], he encountered [[Zameon Gydrael]], a [[Dark Angels|Dark Angel]] seconded to the [[Deathwatch]]; Gydrael was part of a [[Kill-Team]] sent to exterminate the Sslyth before they could disrupt the supply lines of the ongoing [[Vensine Crusade]] but, on seeing one of his [[Chapter|Chapter's]] mortal enemies, Gydrael abandoned his mission and engaged Averamus in a duel.{{Fn|1}}

Neither warrior could land a decisive blow on the other. Eventually the duel was interrupted by [[Xezukoth|Ancient Xezukoth]], an Emperor's Children [[Chaos Dreadnought|Dreadnought]], who attacked Gydrael and tried to devour him. Gydrael survived the attack, but Averamus slipped away in the confusion. Gydrael has since requested that he be allowed to be the one who kills Averamus after the Fallen Angel has been dragged back to [[the Rock]] in chains.{{Fn|1}}

==Appearance & Wargear==
Averamus bore a burn mark on his face in the shape of a hand - this was known by the Dark Angels as the '''Mark of Scorn''', as they believed that [[Lion El'Jonson]] was touching his face as Averamus swore his oaths of loyalty to his [[Primarch]] and that when Averamus betrayed this sacred trust it burned into his flesh. The mark was known to have persisted despite Averamus attempting to repair the damaged flesh multiple times over the years.{{Fn|1}}

In combat, Averamus wielded an archaic pattern of [[power sword]]. His [[power armour]] was the traditional black of the Dark Angels [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]] edged with steel grey and bearing a defaced [[Aquila|Imperial Aquila]] on one pauldron.{{Fn|1}}

==Notes==
Notably, during the duel against Gydrael, Averamus claimed that he was not serving the Emperor's Children or indeed any forces of [[Chaos]] at all. He furthermore told Gydrael that he was actually working to bring down powerful [[Warp]]-spawned enemies of [[Human|mankind]]. Gydrael did not believe any of Averamus's claims, however.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Deathwatch: The Flesh of the Angel (Short Story)|The Flesh of the Angel (Short Story)]] - [[Deathwatch: Ignition (Anthology)]]

