Aye'hal.wikitext:
'''Aye'hal''' is a [[Shas'ui]] in the [[T'au Empire]], who commanded a [[Crisis Battlesuit Team]].{{Fn|1b}}
==History==
In late [[M41]], his [[Stealthsuit Team|Team]] was part of [[Tau Commander|Commander]] [[Braun'wa]]'s forces{{Fn|1b}} that were by the [[T'au Empire]] to "condition" one of the [[Vespid]]'s leadership class strains, while it was in a pupa state. However before the Commander reached its isolated [[Hive]], the pupa was attacked{{Fn|1a}} by the [[Shadow Hawks]] [[Chapter]]{{Fn|1c}} as it was being escorted outside{{Fn|1a}} by the [[Mal'aav]] and [[Mal'bas]],{{Fn|1c}} [[Royal Bodyguard Stingwing]]s{{Fn|1b}}. Led by [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Urotriorchis]],{{Fn|1c}} the [[Space Marines]] had been charged by the [[Ordo Xenos]] with capturing the Vespid leadership pupa, so that the Ordo could study and experiment on it. Thanks to [[Imperial intelligence]],{{Fn|1a}} the Shadow Hawks were aware that Braun'wa was on his way to the Hive and they attempted to complete their mission before the arrival of the Commander.{{Fn|1c}} However Braun'wa and his forces of two [[Crisis Battlesuit Team]]s, led by Aye'hal and [[Shas'ui]] [[Bork'hal]],{{Fn|1b}} reached the Hive before the Space Marines were able to take the pupa from the Royal Stingwings.{{Fn|1c}} Time was now of the essence for both sides, as Braun'wa had to stop the Shadow Hawks before they could escape with the pupa, while the Space Marines had to complete their mission before the T'au Empire could send a larger force against them.{{Fn|1d}}  

Unfortunately for the [[Tau Commander|Commander]], his strike force entered the battle in a piecemeal fashion, instead of as a united front.{{Fn|1c}} Aye'hal's [[Crisis Battlesuit Team|Team]] was the last to arrive{{Fn|1d}} and by then, [[Braun'wa]] and the rest of his forces had been slain by the [[Shadow Hawks]].{{Fn|1c}}{{Fn|1d}} Only the [[Royal Stingwing]] [[Mal'bas]] remained, but together they were able to keep the Space Marines at bay and killed several members of [[Tactical Squad]] '''Butastur'''. which were closest to the pupa. The losses caused the squadron to retreat and with that the Space Marines had run out of time to complete their mission. The Shadow Hawks then made their escape and the pupa was saved. When the battle was over, only one of Aye'hal's Crisis Team members remained alive, though the identity of the survivor is not known.{{Fn|1d}}
==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
[[Braun'wa]] and his forces were created by the [[Games Workshop]] employee [[Marc Raley]]. They were featured on an older version of Games Workshop's website.{{Fn|1b}}
