Azelas Baraxa.wikitext:
{{SonsOfHorusPortal}}
'''Azelas Baraxa''' was a member of the [[Sons of Horus]] during the [[Horus Heresy]].{{Fn|1}}

Baraxa took part in the [[Siege of Terra]]. Following the debacle at the [[Saturnine Wall]] and the death of [[Tormageddon]], Azelas Baraxa was promoted to [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] of the [[2nd Company (Sons of Horus)|2nd Company]]. Unlike many members of the legion by the time of the Siege, Baraxa still held onto the old traditions of [[Cthonia]] and was suspicious of the gifts of [[Chaos]].{{Fn|1a}}

Baraxa was amongst the Sons of Horus captains who actually obeyed [[Abaddon]]'s summons during the final hours of the Siege.{{Fn|2a}} When Abaddon announced his intentions to travel to the ''[[Vengeful Spirit]]'' due to its shields being lowered, Baraxa deferred to the First Captain's authority and urged his colleague [[Lycas Fyton]] to stop antagonizing Abaddon. When that failed, Baraxa instead urged the First Captain to not personally kill Fyton, as it would show a lack of control, and to instead allow [[Hellas Sycar]] to commit the murder for him.{{Fn|2b}}

After arriving on the ''Vengeful Spirit'' alongside Abaddon, Baraxa explored the reality-warped interior of the vessel alongside the First Captain before becoming embattled against maddened [[Word Bearer]] legionaries and [[Solar Auxilia]]. Though they performed well, it took the intervention of [[Erebus]] to stop them being overwhelmed.{{Fn|3}}

Led by Abaddon, Baraxa took part in a Sons of Horus assault on the [[Custodes]] aboard the ''Vengeful Spirit'' under [[Constantin Valdor]].{{Fn|4a}} Baraxa later accompanied Abaddon and other surviving Sons of Horus officers when they finally reached [[Lupercal's Court]] and found [[Garviel Loken]] alongside the body of [[Horus]]. Baraxa moved to attack Loken but was ordered to stand down by Abaddon, and later left the [[Sol System]] aboard the ''Vengeful Spirit''.{{Fn|4b}}

