===Trivia===
{{Trivia}}
*Azrael is named after the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Azrael#Etymology_and_place_in_Judaism Archangel of Death of the same name] in Hebrew and a few select pieces of Islamic lore. From an adapted form of Hebrew it means "Whom God Helps".

====Notes====
*The "Azrael" who currently leads the Dark Angels is not the first Supreme Grand Master whose name was "Azrael". There had been a previous "Supreme Grand Master Azrael" who lead the Dark Angels during the [[Siege of Vraks]]. This is mentioned to the current Azrael by [[Kharn the Betrayer]] during the Pandorax campaign.{{Fn|8}}{{Fn|9}}

