Bail Sharr.wikitext:
{{SpaceMarinesPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is a member of the [[Carcharodons]] [[Space Marine]] [[Chapter]].{{Fn|1a}}

The current Master of the [[3rd Company (Carcharodons)|3rd Company]] of the Chapter, Sharr is known as the '''Reaper Prime'''. He has overseen the 3rd since the 9th century of the [[M41|41st Millennium]] after Master [[Akia]] was killed fighting [[xenos]].{{Fn|1a}}

==Biography==
Sharr was born as '''Caderik''', grandson of a guildmistress on the [[mining world]] of [[Zartak]].{{Fn|2}} 

===Zartak===
[[Image:BailSharr.jpg|thumb|right|220px|3rd Company Master {{PAGENAME}}]]
Shortly upon being appointed command of the 3rd Company, Sharr was embroiled in a plot by the [[Night Lords]] under [[Amon Cull]] and the [[Sorcerer]] [[Shadraith]] to capture a young [[Psyker]] named [[Mika Doren Skell]], intending to use him as a conduit in a ritual to summon the [[Daemon]] [[Bar'ghul]].{{Fn|1a}} The Night Lords are able to board the penal ship ''Imperial Truth'' in pursuit of Skell, then chase him onto the surface of the world of [[Zartak]].{{Fn|1b}} Guided by [[Chief Librarian]] [[Te Kahurangi]], Sharr and the rest of the 3rd arrive in the Zartak System while overseeing a collection of new recruits and [[Chapter Serf]]s dubbed a "Red Tithe". After purging the ''Imperial Truth'' of [[Daemon]]s, Sharr leads a landing on the surface.{{Fn|1c}} In the battle on the mines beneath Zartak, Amon Cull's [[Chaos Raptor]] lieutenant [[Vorfex]] collapses the tunnels upon the Carcharodons. Sharr is saved by [[Company Champion]] [[Red Tane]] as well as the timely arrival of [[1st Company]] Red Brethren [[Terminator]]s under [[Kahu]].{{Fn|1d}}

As Chief Librarian Kahurangi engages in a psychic struggle with Shadraith, the Carcharodons continue to move across the mining complex in search of Skell. During the battle, Kahu and his Red Brethren are killed by [[Warp Talon]]s.{{Fn|1d}} Shadraith is eventually able to capture Skell and prepares him for the binding ritual to serve as the vessel to Bar'ghul in the former [[Arbites]] Precinct Fortress. The Night Lords are able to hold back the Carcharodons with ambushes, tunnel collapses, and waves of [[Cultist]]s and released prisoners.{{Fn|1e}} Shadraith is confronted by Te Kahurangi and the two engage in a psychic battle that sees the Carcharodons Chief Librarian defeated and captured for use in the ritual.{{Fn|1f}} Just as victory seems at hand for the Night Lords, Amon Cull arrives and betrays Shadraith in a bid to be contested ruler of the warband. The interference disrupts the ritual, allowing for Skell to momentarily break free and use Te's [[Force Staff]] to disrupt the [[Void Shield]]s of the Fortress. This allows the Carcharodons under Sharr to launch a teleportation assault.{{Fn|1g}} 

In the final battle inside the Precinct Fortress, Sharr is incapacitated by Cull and saved by Te, who uses his abilities to crush the [[Chaos Lord]] with debris. With their leader dead, Vorfex leads a retreat of the surviving Night Lords. In the aftermath of their victory, the Carcharodons commence their red tithe and take thousands of prisoners, mostly those who had earlier been freed by the Night Lords.{{Fn|1h}} Afterwards, Skell is made into an [[Aspirant]].{{Fn|1i}}

===Ashen Claws===
Te and Sharr were next dispatched to [[Atargatis Prime]] in the [[Ghoul Stars]] in an attempt to find the [[Ashen Claws]].{{Fn|3a}} Meeting with the Ashen Claws [[Chapter Master]] [[Nehat Nev]], Sharr asks for new recruits and fleet support while Nev demands that Lord [[Tyberos]]'s [[Lightning Claw]]s "Hunger" and "Slake", which he considers long-lost relics of the Chapter, be returned in exchange. Sharr refuses, and Nev forces him into a gladiatorial duel against a captured [[World Eater]]. Sharr prevails and is allowed to leave for the ''White Maw'' in orbit, where he learns from Tyberos that a massive [[Tyranid]] fleet is approaching thanks to the presence of a [[Genestealer Cult]] on [[Piety V]]. Sharr is ordered to Piety to eliminate the cult and divert the Tyranids.{{Fn|3b}}

Sharr, the [[Lexicanium]] [[Khauri]], and the 3rd converge on Piety V alongside [[Inquisitor]] [[Nzogwu]] and his retinue, which are investigating attacks against the [[Ecclesiarchy]] leadership there.{{Fn|3c}} Working alongside the Inquisitors, Sharr and his forces are the target of assassination attempts by traitorous [[Frateris Milia]] and respond brutally. Their investigation triggers a full [[Genestealer Cult]] uprising on the world.{{Fn|3d}}

Sharr and the 3rd hold back waves of Genestealer Cultists at the Cathedral of [[Saint Solomon]] as reinforcements arrive in orbit led by the Chapter's [[Battle Barge]]/[[Fortress-Monastery]] ''[[Nicor]]'' under Tyberos himself, which begins to battle arriving Tyranid [[Hive Ship]]s.{{Fn|3e}} As the Imperials seem about to be overwhelmned by the Tyranids, an Ashen Claws fleet arrives and pushes back the [[Xenos]] in orbit. Sharr and Khauri continue their fight on land, and the Lexicanium, revealed to be a vessel for [[Bar'ghul]], kills the [[Genestealer Patriarch]].{{Fn|3f}} In the aftermath, much of the violence is blamed on the Carcharodons, who are blamed for a "massacre" by the sole survivor of Nzogwu's retinue, [[Jade Rannik]].{{Fn|3g}}

==Wargear==
In battle, Sharr wears an ancient suit of [[Mk IV|Mark IV “Maximus” Power Armor]] with a [[Mk III|Mark III "Iron Armour"]] helmet.{{Fn|1a}}

