Bedaris Hyrus.wikitext:
{{SpaceMarinesPortal}}
'''Bedaris Hyrus''' was a [[Silver Templars]] [[Assault Intercessor]] [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]], who took part in the [[Indomitus Crusade]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
He was among his [[Chapter]]'s forces that liberated their future [[Adeptus Astartes Homeworld|Homeworld]] [[Novaris]] and his efforts were honored after the battle. [[Marneus Calgar]] himself presented Hyrus with an ancient [[Ultramarines]] [[boltgun]] and the [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] used the relic as he continued to fight in the [[Indomitus Crusade]]. Sometime later, the [[Silver Templars]] went to the aid of the [[Imperial]] world [[Pendata (World)|Pendata]], which had nearly been overwhelmed by the [[Serpent's Teeth]] [[Chaos Warband|Warband]] and their [[Chaos Cult|Cult]] allies. Three of the Chapter's [[Strike Cruisers]] were sent and they attacked the Warband's flagship, the [[Whisper (Lunar Cruiser)|Whisper]] above Pendata. Unfortunately due to the skill of its [[Chaos Lord|Captain]] [[Krozier Va'kai]] and the fact that the Strike Cruisers did not fight together, the Whisper kept them at bay. However after one of the Strike Cruisers was destroyed, the remaining two Silver Templar warships deployed their forces to Pendata.{{Fn|1}} 

[[Chaos Lord|Captain]] [[Krozier Va'kai|Va'kai]] would warn the Serpent's Teeth of this and the Warband's '''Eighth and Ninth Fang''' squadrons seized a number of [[Hydra Flak Tank]]s. As the [[Silver Templars]]' transports raced towards the [[Chaos Warband|Warband]]'s location, the Fang squadrons opened fire and destroyed several of them. [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] Hyrus was among the many that were able to land, however, and the Silver Templars overwhelmed the two Fang squadrons. With the immediate threat dealt with, the [[Chapter]]'s forces split into squadrons and began hunting for the other members of the [[Serpent's Teeth]]. Hyrus' squadron soon found the Warband's [[Harrowmaster]], [[Drazus Jate]], and his high ranking cohort [[Solomon Akurra]] and the Sergeant gave the order to charge at them. However the two had planted [[Melta Bomb]]s, which exploded when the Silver Templars stepped upon them. This destroyed the legs of most of Hyrus' squadron, leaving only the Sergeant and the squad member [[Jesar]] to attack the two Serpent's Teeth. Hyrus would then fight the Harrowmaster, but was soon overwhelmed by the more skilled Jate. However the Harrowmaster began toying with the Sergeant and after Akurra had killed Jesar, he then severely wounded Hyrus. This angered the Harrowmaster, but Akurra criticized Jate for drawing out the fight and wasting time they did not have. Akurra then claimed he would kill the Sergeant, if the Harrowmaster did not and Jate did so, before Hyrus could reach a [[bolt pistol]].{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Renegades: Harrowmaster (Novel)]], ''Catching Death's Eye''
