Bedwyr.wikitext:
{{ImperialFistsPortal}}
'''Bedwyr''' was a member of the [[Imperial Fists]] [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]], who took part in the [[Horus Heresy]]'s [[Siege of Terra]].{{Fn|1a}}
==History==
He would be among the [[Imperial]] forces that were outside of the [[Imperial Palace]]'s [[Eternity Gate (Imperial)|Eternity Gate]], when it was closed near the end of the [[Siege of Terra|Siege]]. Afterwards, Bedwyr was among the [[Imperial Fists]] that were led by [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Fafnir Rann]]. While they continued to hold their own against the [[Traitor]]s, the Captain's forces were later nearly killed after a surprise attack by a [[Daemon]], disrupted Rann's battle plans. His efforts to hold a position against an oncoming horde were lost because of this and the Captain's forces were only saved due to an intervention by Commander [[Archamus II]]. With the aid of the much larger Imperial force, of Imperial Fists and [[Blood Angels]], the horde was defeated and Rann's forces then joined with the Commander's.{{Fn|1a}}   

This allied force would fight many battles against the [[Traitor]] hordes, which included the defense of the [[Inner Palace]]'s '''Delphine Viaduct'''{{Fn|1b}}. Bedwyr was among [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Fafnir Rann]]'s forces {{Fn|1c}}, which were sent with portions of the [[Blood Angels]] and [[White Scars]] to defend the causeway below the Viaduct{{Fn|1b}}. In the battle that followed, the Traitors swarmed Rann's position and the Imperial Fists Captain [[Fisk Halen]] was nearly slain by the [[Word Bearer]] [[Sor Talgron]]. Rann intervened to save Fisk's life, but was then almost overwhelmed by Talgron himself. This led Bedwyr and the Imperial Fist [[Cortamus]], to come to Rann's aid and the three attacked the Word Bearer together. However Cortamus was quickly killed by Talgron and Bedwyr then used his [[storm shield]] to block the Word Bearer's furious blows. When Rann saw an opportunity to defeat Talgron, Bedwyr once again blocked the Word Bearer from hitting the Captain. This allowed Rann to deliver a series of blows that toppled Talgron and the White Scars then advanced into the Traitors, which caused them to temporarily retreat.{{Fn|1c}} 

==Sources==
*1: [[The End and the Death: Volume I (Novel)]]
