Beldame Sadia.wikitext:
{{ChaosPortal}}
{{DrukhariPortal}}

'''Beldame Sadia''', sometimes known simply as "The Beldame," was the [[xenophile]] leader of a [[Chaos cult]] that plagued the [[Imperium]] for centuries.{{Fn|1a}} 

As a xenophile, her particular fascination was with the [[Dark Eldar]], and she was one of the few [[humans]] to establish compacts with them.  At the time of her location on [[Lethe Eleven]] by [[Inquisitor]] [[Gregor Eisenhorn]], it was rumored that she had become an initiate of the cult of [[Kaela Mensha Khaine]].  Glorying in murder and torture, she recruited her cult exclusively from convicted murderers, and equipped them with [[xenos]] technology, including [[Shadow Field]]s.{{Fn|1b}}

One hundred and fifty years before Eisenhorn's birth, her legs had been destroyed by Inquisitor [[Atelath]], and she had them replaced with a carriage equipped with eight spider-like legs.  She also had [[augmetic]] fangs implanted, and venom sacs in her cheeks that allowed her to spit corrosive poison.{{Fn|1b}}

Eisenhorn tracked her to Lethe Eleven in 338.[[M41]], and interrupted her cult's sacrificial ritual, watched over by an Eldar [[haemonculus]].{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1b}} Beldame attempted to escape, but Eisenhorn disabled her mechanical legs on the roof of the defunct church she was using as a base.  Eisenhorn, crippled by a poison injected by her assistant, [[Pye]], was helpless to stop Beldame from killing him in a last act of spite, but before she could she was killed by [[Arnault Tantalid]], a [[Witch Hunter]] who, ironically, had come to apprehend Eisenhorn.{{Fn|1c}}

