Blikk (Armageddon).wikitext:
{{ImperiumPortal}}
'''Blikk''' is an [[Armageddon]] part-time [[Scout]] and [[Bounty Hunter]], who carries a highly prized [[stasis grenade]], along with a huge array of other weapons.{{Fn|1b}}
==History==
He took part in the [[Third War for Armageddon]] and was the leader of three [[Scout]]s, that had been hired by the [[Mordian 24th]] [[Regiment]].{{Fn|1b}} When it was set to counter-attack against [[Ork]] forces on the '''Sulphur River''', however,{{Fn|1a}} Blikk and the Scouts were left behind with the other civilians attached to the Regiment. Instead, they were placed with [[Imperial Guard Captain|Captain]] [[Kaine (Captain)|Kaine]]'s [[Platoon|3rd Platoon]],{{Fn|1b}} which was charged with guarding the 24th's supplies, within a ruined mine close to the Sulphur River's '''Asch Creek''', until the Regiment returned. Unfortunately disaster struck soon afterwards, when the 24th was almost completely destroyed by an Ork ambush and its few survivors were unable to warn Kaine about their defeat. An Ork [[Warboss]] then led a horde against the unsuspecting Platoon{{Fn|1a}} and Blikk, along with the [[Ratling Sniper]] [[Hookey (Mordian Iron Guard)|Hookey]], Hive Militia and other civilians the 24th left behind as well.{{Fn|1b}} Though vastly outnumbered, the 3rd is unaware that the Orks only have a limited time to battle the Platoon, before the horde has to return to the Xenos' main camp.{{Fn|1a}}
==Trivia==
*The [[Mordian 24th]] were created by the [[Games Workshop]] employee [[Jervis Johnson]]. They were featured in [[Citadel Journal 48]].{{Fn|1a}}
*The ''Last Stand at Asch Creek'' is a modified version of the [[Battle of Glazer's River]] scenario, which appeared in [[White Dwarf 222 (UK)]]. Besides the change in [[Regiment]] and location,{{Fn|1a}} the [[Platoon]] is led by [[Kaine (Captain)|Kaine]], instead of [[Caine (Captain)|Caine]]. The names of the characters Hookey and Blikk, however, remain the same.{{Fn|1b}} 

