Borchu.wikitext:
{{ChaosPortal}}
{{WhiteScarsPortal}}
'''Borchu''' was a [[Space Marine]] of the [[White Scars]] [[Chapter]].{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==
During the [[Hunt for Voldorius]], Borchu was a [[Space Marine Scout|Scout]] serving in a squad under [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] [[Ultas Kholka|Kholka]] as part of [[Task Force Nomad]].{{Fn|2}}

Some time afterwards, Borchu was elevated to the status of [[Battle-Brother]] proper. He was later killed in battle with [[Chaos]] forces on the planet [[Nephis-Ra]]. Afterwards, the enemy recovered his body and used it as a vessel for the [[Daemon]] [[Kagayaga]], who would use it to help in the invasion of the planet [[Tephra VII]]. After the planet fell, Kagayaga was given commanded of the Chaos forces guarding the power plant [[Ignis Mons]]. It was there that the Daemon would fight his personal enemy and Borchu's old friend, [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] [[Kergis]] of the White Scars.{{Fn|1}} Kergis led several [[Space Marines]] into Ignis Mons to destroy the power plant. With its destruction the void shield protecting the main Chaos force was dispelled, allowing the [[Imperial]] forces and White Scars to attack them.{{Fn|1}}

Though Kergis was surprised, he fought the Daemon without holding back, knowing Borchu was truly gone. After a hard fought battle, Kergis managed to behead Borchu's body and send Kagayaga back to the [[warp]]. Afterwards, Kergis and the White Scars under his command destroyed the power plant. When Kergis brought word of his friend's possession back to his Chapter, the record of Borchu’s deeds were quietly purged from the tales the [[Chaplain]]s told to remind the White Scars of their fallen brethren.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
