'''Braun'wa''' was a [[Shas'el]] [[Tau Commander|Commander]]  in the [[T'au Empire]].{{Fn|1b}}
==History==
In late [[M41]], he led{{Fn|1b}} a team that the [[T'au Empire]] had sent to "condition" one of the [[Vespid]]'s leadership class strains, while it was in a pupa state. However before the [[Tau Commander|Commander]] reached its isolated [[Hive]], the pupa was attacked{{Fn|1a}} by the [[Shadow Hawks]] [[Chapter]]{{Fn|1c}} as it was being escorted outside{{Fn|1a}} by the [[Mal'aav]] and [[Mal'bas]],{{Fn|1c}} [[Royal Bodyguard Stingwing]]s{{Fn|1b}}. Led by [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Urotriorchis]],{{Fn|1c}} the [[Space Marines]] had been charged by the [[Ordo Xenos]] with capturing the Vespid leadership pupa, so that the Ordo could study and experiment on it. Thanks to [[Imperial intelligence]],{{Fn|1a}} the Shadow Hawks were aware that Braun'wa was on his way to the Hive and they attempted to complete their mission before the arrival of the Commander.{{Fn|1c}} However Braun'wa and his team of two [[Crisis Battlesuit Team]]s, led by [[Shas'ui]] [[Aye'hal]] and Shas'ui [[Bork'hal]], along with the [[Stealthsuit Team]] of Shas'ui [[Crep'hal]],{{Fn|1b}} reached the Hive before the Space Marines were able to take the pupa from the Royal Stingwings.{{Fn|1c}} Time was now of the essence for both sides, as Braun'wa had to stop the Shadow Hawks before they could escape with the pupa, while the Space Marines had to complete their mission before the T'au Empire could send a larger force against them.{{Fn|1d}}  

Unfortunately for the [[Tau Commander|Commander]], his strike force entered the battle in a piecemeal fashion, instead of as a united front. Braun'wa and [[Crisis Battlesuit Team|Team]] [[Bork'hal]] were the first to arrive and they placed themselves between the [[Shadow Hawks]] and the remnants of the [[Royal Stingwing]]s, guarding the pupa. In the ensuing battle, the Commander was able to temporarily immobilize the [[Castraferrum Dreadnought]] [[Buteogallus]], before the [[Space Marines]] attacked them. Both Braun'wa and Team Bork'hal were quickly killed by the Shadow Hawks, though, with Braun'wa being rammed by [[Tactical Squad]] '''Butastur''''s [[Rhino]], before its [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] struck him down with a [[power fist]].{{Fn|1c}} While most of Braun'wa's remaining forces later died as well,{{Fn|1c}}{{Fn|1d}} their intervention kept the Shadow Hawks at bay long enough, that the Space Marines had no choice but to retreat without the pupa.{{Fn|1d}}
==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
''Braun'wa'' and his forces were created by the [[Games Workshop]] employee [[Marc Raley]]. They were featured on an older version of Games Workshop's website.{{Fn|1b}}

