Bree Jagdea.wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
'''Bree Jagdea'''{{Fn|1b}} was a [[Imperial Guard Commander|Commander]] of the [[Phantine Fighter Corps]] active during the [[Sabbat Worlds Crusade]].{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|2}}

==Biography==
Jagdea was a graduate of the Combat School at [[Hessenville]], and was regarded as one of the finest pilots in the entire corps.{{Fn|1b}}

===Phantine campaign===
[[Image:ICCoverClean.jpg|thumb|right|250px|{{PAGENAME}}{{Fn|3}}]]
She was one of the senior [[Phantine (Planet)|Phantine]] officers involved in the liberation of Phantine itself, after the planet had been subjugated by a force of the [[Blood Pact]] under [[Sagittar Slaith]]. Her wings (including her own personal wing, [[Umbra Flight]]{{Fn|1b}}) were attached to an [[Astra Militarum]] taskforce led by [[Lord General]] [[Barthol Van Voytz|Van Voytz]]; they were responsible for defending the [[drogue]]s used to transport the taskforce across Phantine's cloud oceans and supporting the Crusade's efforts to retake Phantine's vapour mills.{{Fn|1a}}

In the assault on [[Cirenholm]], Jagdea's [[Lightning]] was shot down by the city's defences. She ejected from her plane and landed on the outer hull of Cirenholm, but her blimp-chute only barely deployed in time to prevent her impact from being fatal. Thus, although she had survived, she still sustained a broken arm and multiple broken ribs. Despite this, she was still able to save a Militarum [[drop-ship]] that had veered off course on its approach to its designated drop zone by firing her flare pistol to show its pilot a safe landing area.{{Fn|1b}} The [[Tanith First and Only|Tanith Guardsmen]] onboard the ship, in turn, rescued Jagdea from the outside of the dome she was on, preventing her from freezing to death.{{Fn|1b}}{{Fn|1c}}

After the Imperial victory at Cirenholm, Jagdea's injuries were set. She wasn't cleared to pilot a Lightning until her bones were fully mended, but she still wanted to contribute to the war effort. As a result, she volunteered to pilot one of the [[Marauder Bomber|Marauders]] assigned to [[Operation Larisel]] (a stealth insertion/assassination mission that supported the main Imperial thrust on [[Ouranberg]]). She was assigned to '''Larisel 1''', transporting the Tanith [[Sergeant (Imperial Guard)|Sergeant]] [[Ceglan Varl|Varl]], [[Trooper]] [[Noa Vadim|Vadim]], [[Trooper]] [[Jessi Banda|Banda]] and [[Imperial Guard Scout|Scout-Trooper]] [[Bonin]] and the [[Phantine Skyborne|Skyborne]] [[Corporal]] [[Innis Unterrio|Unterrio]].{{Fn|1d}}

During the insertion, Larisel 1's engines failed as it was two minutes away from its drop zone over Ouranberg. The Guardsmen on board started bailing out and Jagdea's co-pilot was killed by flak shot, but the pilot herself stayed at the controls for as long as possible before bailing out with Bonin.{{Fn|1d}}

===Later Actions===
She survived the conflict and she and a reconstituted Umbra Flight went on to fight in the [[Liberation of Enothis]].{{Fn|2}}

Jagdea later took part in the war for the [[Hive World]] [[Lysander (Hive World)|Lysander]]. By that time, she was considered a former ace fighter pilot and she instead flew supply runs for the [[Imperial]] forces defending the dead [[Hive]] of [[Vesperus]]. However, their [[Chaos]] foes turned it into a war of attrition and this led Jagdea to be later enlisted into the infamous [[Circus 66]] fighter squadron.{{Fn|3}}

