Brey Auerben.wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
'''Brey Auerben''' was a [[Imperial Guard Captain|Captain]] in the [[Tenth Jovani Vanguard]] [[Regiment]], who took part in the [[Sabbat Worlds Crusade]].{{Fn|1a}}
==History==
During the [[Sabbat Worlds Crusade|Crusade]], she was nearly killed on [[Morlond]] after being struck by a pyrochemical blast. Though Auerben survived, the skin on the [[Imperial Guard Captain|Captain]] face was left gnarled from her neck to her cheekbone. She also served in the [[Collegia Tactica]] of the [[Sabbat Worlds Crusade]]'s [[Warmaster]] [[Macaroth]]. This led Auerben to be seconded to the reincarnated [[Imperial Saint]] [[Saint Sabbat|Sabbat]]'s retinue, as her tactical advisor, when the Warmaster and Saint's forces converged on [[Urdesh]]. As the Crusade began to reclaim the [[Forge World]] from the [[Sons of Sek]], however, Macaroth eventually turned Saint Sabbat into a figurehead. The Saint was then kept away in a secret location, but it was discovered by the Sons of Sek. The [[Heretics]] then attempted to kill her, but they were stopped by the [[Iron Snakes]] [[Chapter]], before they reached the Saint. The attack, though, resulted in [[Imperials]] being killed and this quickly spurred Saint Sabbat into taking a more direct role in the battles against the Sons. Auerben and Saint Sabbat's military attache, [[Colonel]] [[Iovin Mazho]], both attempted to dissuade her from this, but the Saint refused and was committed to fighting once again.{{Fn|1b}}

