Brunhildius.wikitext:
{{InquisitionPortal}}
[[Image:Brunhildius1.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Brunhildius{{Fn|1}}]]
'''Brunhildius''' is an [[Inquisition]] [[Acolyte]], whose small size contains an implacable will and iron-hard determination.{{Fn|1}} 
==History==
During her service to the [[Inquisition]], Brunhildius began investigating rumors of a [[Daemon]] that manifested itself across the [[Galaxy]]. This Daemon had in fact, suffered such damage on a now long-forgotten battlefield, that it possessed a ruined portion of a shattered cathedral. This left it anchored eternally to the ragged masonry and the Daemon now travels through time and space via [[Warp]] currents. When it manifests, the possessed portion of the cathedral appears, along with a mangled corpse that has merged with the masonry.{{Fn|1}} 

When her research later proved that the [[Daemon]] actually existed, Brunhildius was given command of an [[Inquisition]] Warband and began pursuing it. The [[Acolyte]]'s forces, however, are mysterious soldiers who wear strange and ancient armor, decorated with relics, triptychs and more. Some say these soldiers are really [[Solar Auxilia]] [[Trooper]]s, who are cursed to travel the [[Warp]] tides in the same manner as the Daemon they are now pursuing{{Fn|1}}. Whatever the truth is, the Auxilia's years-long journey with Brunhildius has left them scarred, both physically and spiritually. This includes the dour [[Imperial Guard Sergeant|Void Sergeant]] who leads them and especially the [[Trooper]] known as the [[Penitent]]. He has suffered greatly during their pursuit of the Daemon and now hides beneath a rough hood, to spare those around him the horror of his visage. Besides the Solar Auxilia, Brunhildius' Warband also include the sinister [[Chiurgeon|Tech-Savant Medicae]], [[Grinvalt]] and a modified [[Scyllax Guardian]], that is charged with protecting her.{{Fn|2}} 
