Brutus Schenker.wikitext:
{{OrdoHereticusPortal}}
'''Brutus Schenker''' is an [[Ordo Hereticus]] [[Inquisitor]], who Inquisitor [[Aurek Herrenvolk]] once served as an [[Interrogator]] to.{{Fn|1a}} 
==History==
He is known to be hands-on in his duties and has a nose for corruption. When it came to fighting the evils of [[Heresy]], Brutus had a common sense, meat-grinder approach to defeating the foes of the [[Imperium]]{{Fn|1a}}. In [[M42]]{{Fn|1b}}, Brutus was conducting [[Psyker|witch]] trials on [[Ergotia]], when his [[123rd Pontifical Strikes]] [[Inquisitorial Stormtrooper]] detail was suddenly pulled from him by his superiors. The Inquisitor's former [[Interrogator]] [[Aurek Herrenvolk]] was about to conduct an investigation into [[Chaos Cult|Cult]] spree killings within the [[Spetzghast System]] and had requested a detachment of Stormtroopers to aid him. As Aurek's needs were deemed to be greater and that he also out-ranked Brutus, their was nothing the Inquisitor could do to stop the Pontificals from leaving. After they departed, Brutus was left with just his retinue and some local high-plains muscle to continue conducting the trials with.{{Fn|1a}}

