{{NurglePortal}}
{{ambig|subject=the character|disambiguation=Bubonicus}}
[[File:Bubonicus.jpg|right|thumb|150px|'''Lothar Bubonicus''' as a mortal Champion of Nurgle]]
'''Lothar''' (now known as '''Bubonicus''' and the [[Daemon#Daemonic_Names|daemonic name]] ''Ghur'urgh bu'yue''){{Fn|1a}} was a mortal [[Champion of Nurgle]], born on a backwards planet which remains cut off from the [[Imperium]] by [[warp storm]]s. 

Raised to [[daemonhood]], he now rules a [[daemon world]] within the [[Eye of Terror]], also named [[Bubonicus (Planet) |Bubonicus]].{{Fn|1b}}{{Fn|2}}

During the [[Horus Heresy]], Bubonicus was one of many [[daemon]]s summoned by [[Erebus]], [[First Chaplain]] of the [[Word Bearers]], by a dark ritual conducted during the [[Battle of Calth]], presumably as a prelude to [[Horus]]'s attack on the [[Imperial Palace]] during the [[Battle of Terra]].{{Fn|3}}

==Trivia==
{{trivia}}
=== Warhammer World within the 40K Galaxy ===
In  [[Realm of Chaos: The Lost and the Damned]] Bubonicus is shown in the Warhammer Fantasy section as an example of the rules for Chaos Champion's gifts and warbands. It ends with Lothar becoming the Daemon Prince Ghur'urgh bu'yue known as Bubonicus.{{Fn|1a}} 

Bubonicus is then mentioned again within the 40K section ''"Another world has boiling lakes of blood from which spheres of fire float into the sky and spread their light across the firmament - the rule of this world is the Daemon Prince Bubonicus, formely a mortal Champion of Nurgle on one of the myriad lost worlds in the galaxy"'' {{Fn|1b}}. This exact line is repeated in [[Codex: Chaos (2nd Edition)]]{{Fn|2}} 

[[Realm of Chaos: The Lost and the Damned]] specifically mentions ''"The Warhammer World is bound by storms of magic so that it remains isolated from the other worlds of the human galaxy".''{{Fn|1c}}

