[[Image:Bubonis.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Bubonis{{Fn|1}}]]
'''Bubonis''' is a [[Nurgle]] [[Daemon Prince]], who is merged with a [[Chaos Warlord Titan]] and he commands the [[Festering Death]] [[Traitor Titan Legion]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
Once known as [[Grand Master (Collegia Titanica)|Grand Master]] '''Marnic Bubon''', he led the '''Silver Scythes''' [[Titan Legion]], during the [[Great Crusade]]. When the [[Horus Heresy]] began, the Scythes were located in the rim of [[Imperial]] space and were far from the fighting that took place. However, the Titan Legion quickly succumbed to the lure of the [[Chaos God]] [[Nurgle]] and became the [[Festering Death]]. They then joined the traitorous [[Warmaster]]'s forces and would win their new master's favor, leading Bubon to become the [[Daemon Prince]] '''Bubonis''', after becoming merged with the [[Warlord Titan]] he commanded. However once Warmaster [[Horus]] was slain, Bubonis and the Festering Death joined the Warmaster's forces that fled to the [[Eye of Terror]]. The Daemon Prince now waits there, for the opportunity to seek his revenge against the Imperium.{{Fn|1}} 
==Abilities==
In his [[Chaos Titan]] form, Bubonis is armed with a [[Rot Spitter]], [[Corrupting Spittle]] and both arms wield the [[Claws of Nurgle]]. The [[Daemon Prince]]'s body protrudes gaping mouthed tentacles, which shoot out gooey rot and his body's huge gaping mouth spits out long streams of corrupted slime. Bubonis also leaves a trail of sticky contagious slime behind him as well and also wields a special [[Plague Cannon]] that [[Nurgle]] awarded the Daemon Prince, 1200 years ago. This mighty weapon is gripped by the Claws of Nurgle, but Bubonis is unable to use them both at once.{{Fn|1}}
==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
''Bubonis'' and the [[Festering Death]] were created by the [[Games Workshop]] employee [[James Funnell]]. They appeared in [[The Citadel Journal 9]].{{Fn|1}}

