'''Bulveye Greybeard'''{{Fn|5a}}, known as the '''Old Wolf''', is the [[Wolf Lord|Jarl]] of Dekk-Tra, the [[Space Wolves]]' [[13th Great Company]], who led them into the [[warp]] after the [[Battle of Prospero]]. Like many of the 13th Great Company, Bulveye suffered from the [[Wulfen|Curse of the Wulfen]].{{Fn|2}}

===Biography===
Bulveye was one of the 'Old Guard', the older Legionaries of Dekk-Tra that fought alongside [[Leman Russ (Primarch)|Leman Russ]] on [[Fenris]] before the coming of the [[Emperor|Allfather]].{{Fn|2}} He was the Huscarl of [[Wolf Lord|Jarl]] [[Jorin Bloodhowl]]'s [[Wolf Guard]] at the time of the [[Dulan Campaign]].{{Fn|4a}}

Later in the [[Great Crusade]], Bulveye succeeded Bloodhowl as Jarl of the 13th Great Company, known as the '''Wolf Brothers''', and commanded the [[954th Expeditionary Fleet]]. He led Imperial forces in the [[Battle of Kernunnos]]{{Fn|1}} and later fought in the [[Burning of Prospero]], at the end of which he led his Great Company into the [[warp]] in pursuit of the surviving [[Thousand Sons]].{{Fn|2}}

Nearly ten thousand years later, he fought alongside [[Ragnar Blackmane]] on the "shadow" of [[Charys]] to prevent the [[Sorcerer]] [[Madox]] from completing a ritual to destroy the Space Wolves using the [[Spear of Russ]].{{Fn|3}}

Bulveye and his two hundred surviving brothers of the 13th were eventually recovered on [[Prospero]] by the Space Wolves under [[Njal Stormcaller]], discovering that ten thousand years had past and it was now the [[42nd Millennium]]. Though now an ancient relic, Bulveye expressed his desire to once again take the war to the Sons of [[Magnus]].{{Fn|5b}}

===Wargear===
Bulveye carried a [[chainsword]] in the Dulan Campaign.{{Fn|4b}} He later wielded ''[[eldingverfall]]'' — "the storm's strike" - a rune-inscribed [[power axe]] with a haft bound in sealskin.{{fn|2}}

