'''Buri Aegnirssen the Thrice-Devoured''' is a [[Leagues of Votann]] [[Kin (Leagues of Votann)|Kin]] who is the last survivor of the [[Emberg-Aegnir Bloc]] [[League (Leagues of Votann)|League]].{{Fn|1}}

===History===
No coherent account exists for Buri's past before he took up his quest of vengeance.{{Fn|3a}} What is known is that Buri's League was devoured by [[Hive Fleet Leviathan]] and he bears the scars, sorrow and bitterness of their loss. During its destruction, the League fought to the bitter end to defend their [[Ancestor Core]]. In the aftermath the core was driven insane and is now known as the [[Mad Core]]. Buri was the sole survivor and has sought vengeance against the [[Tyranids]] ever since.{{Fn|2}}

Buri first appeared in Kin history when he fought alongside [[Kindred Deep-Seven]] of the [[Greater Thurian League]], arriving on an acid-ravaged scout ship as the Kindred fought to evacuate in the face of a Tyranid splinter fleet at the [[Battle of the Gnawed Reach]]. Leading a group of warriors from various Kindred's, Buri roared an unknown war song as he plunged into the Tyranid swarms. At the climax of the battle, he sought out the leader-beast of the Tyranid swarm and threw himself into its maw. Though thought killed, Buri suddenly hacked his way out of the creature's throat in a gush of ichor. The act exemplified the supernatural resilience and ferocity of Buri, and his presence was able to rally the Kin to drive off the orbiting [[Bio-Ship]]s and slaughter the remaining Tyranids on the surface. Survivors later described him as a manifestation of the [[Ancestor Core|Votann]]'s will.{{Fn|3a}}

Since then, Buri has been sighted across League territories and the frontiers of far-space. Though he speaks not of his past, other Kin believe he is attempting to balance the debt incurred when his league fell. He is a scarred and at times unhinged warrior who negotiates transportation from one war zone to the next, usually at ones involving the Tyranids. His obsession and frenzied recklessness has led some Kin to become wary and distrustful of his presence, though they still see his worth in times of war.{{Fn|3a}}

In battle, Buri wields the [[Darkstar Glaive]] [[Bane (Darkstar Glaive)|Bane]]. He is a ferocious fighter that is notoriously difficult to kill and can be spotted by the [[Tyranid]] skull he wears as a trophy.{{Fn|1}}

