Burning Princess.wikitext:
{{ChaosPortal}}
The '''Burning Princess''' is an [[The Assignment#List of psionic levels|alpha-plus level]] [[Rogue Psyker]] in the [[Calixis Sector]], who is known mostly for [[Pyromancy]].{{Fn|2}}

In 656.[[M41]], she appeared to be a bald-headed woman in her late teens.{{Fn|2}}

==History==
According to damaged records, a nine year-old child named Lottie (surname unknown) manifested powerful pyrokinetic abilities. A [[witch hunter]] team was sent to collect her for the [[Black Ships]], but all records of the results of that mission were destroyed.{{Fn|1}}
A pyrokinetic girl with a witch hunter's brand on her cheek{{Fn|3}} was involved in a rebellion on [[Pellucida IX]], which brought her to the attention of the [[Ordo Hereticus]].{{Fn|2}} Since then, she has worked alongside the pirates of the ''[[Storm Walker (Pirate Ship)|Storm Walker]]''{{Fn|1}} in the [[Hazeroth Abyss]],{{Fn|3}} the [[mutant]]s of the [[Stigmatus Covenant]], a variety of violent rebellious & heretical groups,{{Fn|2}} and is thought to have been the one who burned down [[Acreage]]'s '''Cathedral Mount''', which killed ten thousand pilgrims and citizens of the world, including all of the senior clergy.{{Fn|1}} The Burning Princess also killed the Ordo Hereticus [[Inquisitor]] [[Fhendahl]] on [[Dusk]], as well as the specially equipped taskforce he used in his failed attempt to apprehend the [[Rogue Psyker]]. Rumours of a 'burning woman' taking part in civil unrest on [[St. Astrid's Fall]] in 656.M41 merited an [[Inquisitor]]ial agent being sent after her, but all contact with said agent was lost{{Fn|2}}

She was originally listed as a low alpha level psyker, but that was quickly upgraded to alpha-plus level, prompting fears that she will continue to grow more powerful as she ages.{{Fn|2}}

She appears to be a loner, though she works as a mercenary for heretics, mutants, and pirates, seemingly at random, wandering the Calixis Sector with no apparent aim, or motivation.{{Fn|1}} Survivors of her attacks confusingly report her as being alternately a jaded, dead-eyed puppet of a person, or a maniacal malicious sadist, laughing at the pain and death that she inflicts.{{Fn|3}}

