Buteogallus.wikitext:
{{UltramarinesPortal}}
'''Buteogallus''' is a [[Castraferrum Dreadnought]] in the [[Shadow Hawks]] [[Chapter]].{{Fn|1b}}
==History==
In late [[M41]], the [[Shadow Hawks]]{{Fn|1b}} were tasked by the [[Ordo Xenos]] with capturing one of the [[Vespid]]'s leader strains that was still in its pupa stage.{{Fn|1a}} Urotriorchis was charged with carrying out the mission, with Buteogallus and the [[Tactical Squads]] '''Accipiter''' and '''Butastur'''.{{Fn|1b}} [[Imperial intelligence]] had provided the location of the pupa's isolated [[Vespid Hive]] to the Ordo, as well as that it was being taken outside to undergo "conditioning" at the hands of a team sent by the [[T'au Empire]].{{Fn|1a}} The team was led by the [[Shas'el]] [[Tau Commander|Commander]] [[Braun'wa]]{{Fn|1c}} and the Shadow Hawks knew he would be minutes away from reaching the pupa, when they began their mission. This meant they only had a short window to capture it, before the T'au Empire gained possession of the pupa{{Fn|1a}} or assembled a large force that would overwhelm the Shadow Hawks.{{Fn|1d}} 

With the element of surprise on their side, though, Buteogallus was able to inflict heavy losses to the [[Mal'bas]] and [[Mal'aav]] [[Royal Bodyguard Stingwing]]s, that were guarding the pupa. However the [[Shadow Hawks]] were unable to claim it from the surviving Stingwings before [[Tau Commander|Commander]] [[Braun'wa]]'s forces arrived at the [[Vespid Hive|Hive]]. Fortunately for the [[Space Marines]], they did so in a piecemeal fashion and Braun'wa along with most of his forces were slain.{{Fn|1c}} Buteogallus played a key part in the battle, as the [[Castraferrum Dreadnought|Dreadnought]] killed many of the [[Xenos]].{{Fn|1c}}{{Fn|1d}} While the Shadow Hawks suffered little loses in return, the Commander's intervention kept Urotriorchis' forces at bay long enough to prevent the Space Marines from capturing the pupa. With their time to complete the mission over, the Shadow Hawks had no choice but to retreat before more of the T'au Empire's forces arrived. Though they were able to escape, the [[Ordo Xenos]] were not pleased to learn of Urotriorchis' failure.{{Fn|1d}}
==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
[[Urotriorchis]] and his forces were created by the [[Games Workshop]] employee [[Jeff Hall]]. They were featured on an older version of Games Workshop's website.{{Fn|1b}}

