Calladayce Taurovalia Kesh.wikitext:
{{AdeptusCustodesPortal}}
'''Calladayce Taurovalia Kesh''' is an [[Adeptus Custodes]] who has been chosen to take part in the [[Blood Games]] several times due to her flair for the grandiose and unexpected.{{Fn|1}}
==History==
In her last [[Blood Game]] in [[M42]], Kesh attempted to win by [[teleport]]ing a compact [[Cyclonic Torpedo|cyclonic warhead]] next to the [[Emperor]]'s [[Golden Throne]]. She was going to accomplish this via the [[Battlefleet Solar]] [[Cobra Destroyer]] [[Vigilant Flame]], which she had commandeered. Due to her being a member of the [[Adeptus Custodes]], the Vigilant Flame's crew obediently followed her orders to travel to [[Terra]] so she could complete her mission. Having been sworn to secrecy, they even repeated her concocted cover story - that they were transporting an attache from the [[Hive World]] [[Necromunda (planet)|Necromunda]] - to get past the Throne World's defenses. Though they were doubtful about doing what Kesh ordered, none of the crew disobeyed her, save for the Vigilant's [[Vox|Officer of Vox]] [[Ewa Bhattoor]]. She began discreetly sending out a distress signal, which was received by the Custodes watching over Terra. Soon [[Shield-Captain]] [[Nicodaemius]] would teleport aboard the Vigilant with a group of Custodes and confront his friend Kesh. With that, the Vigilant was stopped from delivering its deadly cargo and Kesh's part in the Blood Games was over. This was eight-hundred and seventy three days, sixteen hours, and nine minutes after it began.{{Fn|1}}

==Notes==
Calladayce Taurovalia Kesh and [[Bayezara Aggonades]] are the first Custodes referred to as female, a concept which first appeared in the [[10th Edition]] codex.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Codex: Adeptus Custodes (10th Edition)]], pgs. 14-15 - via [https://www.belloflostsouls.net/2024/04/warhammer-40k-female-adeptus-custodes-confirmed.html Bell of Lost Souls article (Posted on 14/04/2024)] (Last accessed on 18/04/2024)
