Captain Catachan.wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
[[Image:Captain Catachan.jpg|thumb|right|200px|The picture of Captain Catachan, used by [[The Regimental Standard]]{{Fn|1}}]]
'''Captain Catachan''' is a [[Catachan Jungle Fighters]] [[Imperial Guard Captain|Captain]] and a hero of the [[Imperium]].{{Fn|1}}

==History==
Among his exploits are single-handedly defeating the [[Hrud]] invasion of [[Delphion V]], being instrumental in the destruction of the notorious [[Ork]] [[Gargant]] [[Morkthunder]], and becoming the only documented [[human]] to ever headbutt a [[Carnifex]] to death. Captain Catachan is also considered by [[The Regimental Standard]] to be the living embodiment of the [[Astra Militarum]]'s martial prowess. This led the captain to be asked to write a guest column about tips for [[guardsmen]] fighting in the [[death world]] jungles of [[Krylux V]]. Catachan noted in the column that he was expected to turn its readers into expert jungle fighters. While he never shied away from a hopeless battle, the captain was sure most of the guardsmen reading the column would still die. However, he would then give several detailed tips on how the guardsmen could avoid that fate. Catachan then ended the column by stating if the guardsmen survived long enough, he would write another column and share his recipe for heavy flamer-barbecued [[Catachan Devil]].{{Fn|1}} 

While [[The Regimental Standard]] warned its readers against following some of the captain's tips{{Fn|1}}, it was very popular. Due to [[guardsmen]] asking for him to return, Catachan was asked to write a guide on dangerous [[death world]] flora. His advice was to simply avoid going near them or burn the flora with [[promethium]] before carefully advancing. The captain would end the column, however, by stating its readers should leave the real jungle fighting to experts.{{Fn|2}}

